## Excalidraw-Specific Risks

Excalidraw's core functionality involves rendering user-created content (SVG, canvas elements, imported files) and handling real-time collaboration. These capabilities introduce unique security considerations beyond generic web security.

### SVG & Canvas Rendering Security

**Risk**: User-supplied drawing data and imported SVG/library files can contain malicious payloads that execute when rendered or processed.

**Mitigations**:

```typescript
// ❌ BAD - Unvalidated SVG rendering
const renderImportedSVG = (svgString: string) => {
  const container = document.createElement('div');
  container.innerHTML = svgString; // XSS vector
  return container;
};

// ✅ GOOD - Sanitized SVG processing
import DOMPurify from 'dompurify';

const renderImportedSVG = (svgString: string) => {
  // Sanitize SVG to remove event handlers and scripts
  const safeSVG = DOMPurify.sanitize(svgString, {
    ALLOWED_TAGS: ['svg', 'g', 'rect', 'circle', 'path', 'ellipse', 'polyline', 'polygon', 'line', 'text', 'tspan', 'image', 'defs', 'linearGradient', 'radialGradient', 'stop', 'pattern', 'marker', 'filter', 'feGaussianBlur', 'feColorMatrix'],
    ALLOWED_ATTR: ['x', 'y', 'width', 'height', 'cx', 'cy', 'r', 'd', 'points', 'fill', 'stroke', 'viewBox', 'preserveAspectRatio', 'id', 'href', 'xlink:href', 'opacity', 'transform', 'font-size', 'font-family', 'text-anchor'],
    KEEP_CONTENT: true,
  });
  const container = document.createElement('div');
  container.innerHTML = safeSVG;
  return container;
};
```

**Excalidraw-Specific Checks**:

- [ ] **SVG imports sanitized**: Verify `DOMPurify` is used for all imported SVG/library files (search: `innerHTML` in rendering paths)
- [ ] **Canvas API safe**: Verify no `eval()`, `Function()`, or dynamic code in canvas manipulation
- [ ] **Library file validation**: Check that `.excalidraw` and `.excalidrawlib` imports validate structure before processing
- [ ] **Element schema enforced**: Validate imported elements conform to `ExcalidrawElement` schema (type, id, position, size)
- [ ] **No innerHTML for SVG**: Search for `innerSVG` or `innerHTML` patterns in element rendering; use canvas API or DOM APIs with sanitized content

### .excalidraw & Library File Security

**Risk**: `.excalidraw` files (JSON format) and library files can be manipulated to include arbitrary payloads in element metadata, custom properties, or malformed structures.

**Mitigations**:

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD - Validate .excalidraw file structure
import { ExcalidrawElement } from '@excalidraw/element';

const importDrawingFile = async (file: File): Promise<DrawingData> => {
  if (!file.name.endsWith('.excalidraw')) {
    throw new Error('Invalid file type: expected .excalidraw');
  }
  
  if (file.size > 50 * 1024 * 1024) { // 50MB limit
    throw new Error('File too large');
  }
  
  const text = await file.text();
  let data: unknown;
  
  try {
    data = JSON.parse(text);
  } catch (e) {
    throw new Error('Malformed JSON in .excalidraw file');
  }
  
  // Validate structure against schema
  if (!isValidDrawingData(data)) {
    throw new Error('Invalid drawing data structure');
  }
  
  // Sanitize all text-like fields in elements
  const elements = (data.elements as ExcalidrawElement[]).map(el => ({
    ...el,
    text: sanitizeText(el.text || ''),
    customData: sanitizeCustomData(el.customData),
  }));
  
  return { ...data, elements };
};

const isValidDrawingData = (data: unknown): data is DrawingData => {
  if (typeof data !== 'object' || data === null) return false;
  
  const obj = data as Record<string, unknown>;
  if (!Array.isArray(obj.elements)) return false;
  if (obj.appState && typeof obj.appState !== 'object') return false;
  
  return true;
};

const sanitizeText = (text: string): string => {
  // Remove null bytes and excessive whitespace
  return text.replace(/\x00/g, '').slice(0, 10000);
};

const sanitizeCustomData = (customData: unknown): Record<string, unknown> | null => {
  if (!customData || typeof customData !== 'object') return null;
  // Only allow safe JSON-serializable types
  try {
    return JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(customData));
  } catch {
    return null;
  }
};
```

**Excalidraw-Specific Checks**:

- [ ] **File format validated**: `.excalidraw` and `.excalidrawlib` files checked before import (file extension, JSON parsing, schema validation)
- [ ] **Element array schema enforced**: All elements validated against `ExcalidrawElement` type; required fields present (id, type, x, y, width, height)
- [ ] **Custom properties sanitized**: Any user-defined custom data in elements is parsed safely without code execution
- [ ] **File size limits enforced**: Drawing files limited to reasonable size (e.g., 50MB) to prevent DoS
- [ ] **Restore function isolated**: Verify `packages/excalidraw/data/restore.ts` validates all restored data (protected file — changes require full test suite)

### CSP (Content Security Policy) Configuration

**Risk**: Without proper CSP headers, embedded iframes, external scripts, and inline styles can be injected or executed maliciously.

**Mitigations**:

```
# ✅ GOOD - Strict CSP for Excalidraw app
Content-Security-Policy: 
  default-src 'self'; 
  script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; 
  style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; 
  img-src 'self' data: https:; 
  font-src 'self' data:; 
  connect-src 'self' https: wss:; 
  frame-ancestors 'none'; 
  base-uri 'self'; 
  form-action 'self';
```

**Rationale**:
- `script-src 'wasm-unsafe-eval'` — Required for Excalidraw's WASM optimizations
- `style-src 'unsafe-inline'` — Required for dynamic canvas styling (review if component-based styling is possible)
- `frame-ancestors 'none'` — Prevents embedding in cross-origin iframes (protects against clickjacking)
- `connect-src wss:` — Required for WebSocket real-time collaboration
- `img-src data:` — Allows inline data URIs for exported drawings

**Excalidraw-Specific Checks**:

- [ ] **CSP frame-ancestors set**: Verify header includes `frame-ancestors 'none'` or restricted origins only
- [ ] **CSP script-src configured**: Check that `'wasm-unsafe-eval'` is used if WASM is enabled, no `'unsafe-eval'`
- [ ] **CSP connect-src allows WebSocket**: Verify `wss:` is included for real-time collaboration
- [ ] **No unsafe-inline scripts**: Search for `<script>` tags with inline code; use `<script src>` only
- [ ] **CSP headers tested**: Verify no console errors for CSP violations in browser DevTools

### Real-Time Collaboration & E2E Encryption

**Risk**: Real-time collaboration via WebSocket/Firebase can expose user drawing data in transit and at rest. Untrusted clients can inject malicious changes.

**Mitigations**:

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD - E2E encryption for collaboration
import { encrypt, decrypt } from '@excalidraw/crypto';

const sendCollaborationUpdate = async (
  update: ExcalidrawChange,
  roomId: string,
  encryptionKey: string
) => {
  // Encrypt before sending
  const encrypted = await encrypt(JSON.stringify(update), encryptionKey);
  
  await firebaseDb.collection('rooms').doc(roomId).collection('changes').add({
    encrypted,
    timestamp: serverTimestamp(),
    clientId: generateClientId(),
  });
};

const receiveCollaborationUpdate = async (
  encryptedUpdate: string,
  encryptionKey: string
): Promise<ExcalidrawChange> => {
  // Decrypt and validate
  const decrypted = await decrypt(encryptedUpdate, encryptionKey);
  const update = JSON.parse(decrypted);
  
  // Validate update structure
  if (!isValidExcalidrawChange(update)) {
    throw new Error('Invalid collaboration update');
  }
  
  return update;
};
```

**Excalidraw-Specific Checks**:

- [ ] **E2E encryption enabled for real-time rooms**: Verify all WebSocket/Firebase collaboration uses encryption
- [ ] **Room encryption key management**: Check that encryption keys are generated per room and never logged or exposed
- [ ] **Update validation**: Verify all received collaboration updates are validated before applying to app state
- [ ] **Client ID tracking**: Ensure client IDs are generated securely and cannot be spoofed
- [ ] **Timestamp verification**: Check that server-generated timestamps are used to prevent replay attacks
- [ ] **Rate limiting on updates**: Verify real-time updates are rate-limited per client to prevent DoS

### Firebase & Backend Security

**Risk**: Firebase Realtime Database and Cloud Firestore can expose drawing data if security rules are misconfigured. Unauthorized clients can read/write other users' data.

**Mitigations** (Firebase Security Rules):

```
// ✅ GOOD - Firestore security rules for Excalidraw collaboration
rules_version = '2';
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {
    match /rooms/{roomId} {
      // Only allow owner or invited collaborators
      allow read, write: if request.auth != null && 
        (resource.data.owner == request.auth.uid || 
         request.auth.uid in resource.data.collaborators);
    }
    
    match /rooms/{roomId}/changes/{changeId} {
      // Allow reading if user is collaborator
      allow read: if request.auth != null &&
        exists(/databases/$(database)/documents/rooms/$(roomId)) &&
        (get(/databases/$(database)/documents/rooms/$(roomId)).data.owner == request.auth.uid ||
         request.auth.uid in get(/databases/$(database)/documents/rooms/$(roomId)).data.collaborators);
      
      // Only allow appending, never update or delete
      allow create: if request.auth != null &&
        request.resource.data.clientId == request.auth.uid &&
        request.resource.data.roomId == roomId;
      
      allow delete: if false; // Never allow deletion of history
    }
  }
}
```

**Excalidraw-Specific Checks**:

- [ ] **Firebase rules enforce ownership**: Verify owner and collaborator checks on all read/write operations
- [ ] **Collaboration updates append-only**: Check that changes are created (not updated) to maintain immutable history
- [ ] **Room encryption keys in app only**: Verify encryption keys are NOT stored in Firebase; generated client-side
- [ ] **User authentication required**: Confirm all database rules check `request.auth != null`
- [ ] **Rate limiting configured**: Check Firebase has rate-limit rules or Cloud Functions to prevent document write spam
- [ ] **Data retention policy**: Verify old change records are archived or deleted per compliance requirements

