## How to Verify

### Code Review Checklist (Generic)

- [ ] **User inputs checked**: All `userInput`, `URLParams`, `query parameters`, `file uploads` are validated
- [ ] **No innerHTML with user data**: Search for `innerHTML +=`, `innerHTML =` patterns
- [ ] **No eval/dynamic code**: No `eval()`, `new Function()`, `setInterval(code)` with user input
- [ ] **Secrets not exposed**: No API keys in code, `console.log()` calls don't leak sensitive data
- [ ] **CSRF protection**: State-changing requests include CSRF tokens
- [ ] **File uploads validated**: Size, type, and content checked before processing
- [ ] **Dependencies audited**: Run `yarn audit` before merge, no high/critical vulnerabilities
- [ ] **API endpoints protected**: Authentication/authorization checked server-side

### Excalidraw-Specific Code Review Checklist

- [ ] **SVG/innerHTML scanning**: Run search patterns below; verify all SVG rendering uses DOMPurify sanitization
- [ ] **innerSVG safety**: Search for `innerSVG` patterns; ensure no user content directly set on SVG elements
- [ ] **File import validation**: Verify `.excalidraw`, `.excalidrawlib` imports validate JSON structure and element schema
- [ ] **Library element schema**: Check imported library elements conform to `ExcalidrawElement` type (required: id, type, x, y, width, height)
- [ ] **Custom data sanitization**: Verify custom properties in elements are JSON-safe and don't contain code
- [ ] **CSP headers present**: Check production app headers include `frame-ancestors 'none'` and `script-src` restrictions
- [ ] **E2E encryption enforced**: Verify real-time collaboration uses encryption; room keys never logged or stored server-side
- [ ] **Firebase rules audited**: Confirm ownership and collaborator checks; rules prevent unauthorized access
- [ ] **No restore.ts changes**: Verify `packages/excalidraw/data/restore.ts` (protected file) unchanged unless with full test suite
- [ ] **Renderer security**: Verify `packages/excalidraw/scene/Renderer.ts` uses safe rendering methods; no innerHTML in render pipeline

### Automated Checks (Generic)

```bash
# Check for security vulnerabilities in dependencies
yarn audit

# Search for dangerous patterns
rg "innerHTML\s*=" packages/ --type ts --type tsx
rg "eval\(" packages/ --type ts --type tsx
rg "new Function\(" packages/ --type ts --type tsx
```

### Automated Checks (Excalidraw-Specific)

```bash
# 1. SVG rendering security - search for innerHTML/innerSVG patterns in rendering code
rg "innerHTML\s*=" packages/excalidraw/scene/ --type ts --type tsx
rg "innerSVG\s*=" packages/excalidraw/ --type ts --type tsx

# 2. Sanitization verification - confirm DOMPurify usage in SVG/import paths
rg "DOMPurify\.sanitize" packages/excalidraw/ --type ts --type tsx

# 3. File import validation - check .excalidraw/.excalidrawlib parsing
rg "\.excalidraw|\.excalidrawlib|importDrawing|importLibrary" packages/excalidraw/actions/ --type ts --type tsx | head -20

# 4. Element schema validation - search for type checking on imported elements
rg "ExcalidrawElement|isValidElement|validateElement" packages/excalidraw/actions/ --type ts --type tsx | head -20

# 5. Restore function inspection (protected file - reference only)
ls -la packages/excalidraw/data/restore.ts

# 6. Renderer inspection (protected file - reference only)
ls -la packages/excalidraw/scene/Renderer.ts

# 7. Real-time collaboration - verify encryption usage
rg "encrypt|E2E|collaborat" packages/excalidraw/collaboration/ --type ts --type tsx

# 8. Firebase rules audit - check security rules configuration
find . -name "firestore\.rules" -o -name "*firebase*rules*" -type f | head -10

# 9. CSP header verification - check web app configuration
rg "Content-Security-Policy|frame-ancestors|script-src" excalidraw-app/ --type ts --type tsx --type js --type json | head -20

# 10. Custom data handling - search for metadata/customData processing
rg "customData|metadata|\.data\[" packages/excalidraw/actions/ --type ts --type tsx | head -20
```

### Testing (Generic)

- [ ] Attempt to inject XSS payloads: `<img src=x onerror=alert(1)>`
- [ ] Test with invalid/oversized file uploads
- [ ] Verify CSRF tokens are present in forms
- [ ] Check that auth tokens are not logged or exposed in network tab
- [ ] Validate that API rejects requests without proper authorization

### Testing (Excalidraw-Specific)

**SVG/Rendering Security**:
- [ ] Attempt to import SVG with event handlers: `<svg onload=alert(1)><circle onclick=alert(2)></svg>` — verify no execution
- [ ] Import SVG with script tags: `<svg><script>alert('xss')</script></svg>` — verify script is stripped
- [ ] Import SVG with data URIs: `<svg><image href="data:text/html,<script>alert(1)</script>"></image></svg>` — verify sanitized

**File Import Security**:
- [ ] Import `.excalidraw` file with malformed JSON — verify error handling
- [ ] Import `.excalidraw` with oversized drawing (100MB+) — verify size limit enforced
- [ ] Import `.excalidraw` with invalid element schema (missing required fields) — verify validation rejects
- [ ] Import library with custom data containing code: `"customData": {"fn": "alert(1)"}` — verify it's not executed
- [ ] Import `.excalidrawlib` with modified type declarations — verify schema enforcement

**Real-Time Collaboration**:
- [ ] Send unencrypted collaboration update on a room with E2E encryption enabled — verify rejection
- [ ] Attempt to modify other user's updates in real-time room — verify permission denied
- [ ] Send collaboration update with spoofed clientId — verify server rejects
- [ ] Check network traffic for encryption of drawing data — verify no plaintext exposure

**CSP Compliance**:
- [ ] Open app in browser; check DevTools Console for CSP violations — should be none
- [ ] Attempt to load external scripts via iframe injection — verify blocked by `frame-ancestors 'none'`
- [ ] Verify WebSocket connections to collaboration server use `wss://` (not `ws://`)

**Firebase Security**:
- [ ] Attempt to read another user's private drawing room via Firestore — verify denied
- [ ] Attempt to delete historical changes in a shared room — verify Firebase rules reject delete
- [ ] Check that encryption keys are never stored or logged in Firebase — verify key management is client-only

